WEBVTT

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.940
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.820
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.660
but also in crime.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.780
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.490
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.260
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:49.940
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:55.320
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:02.080
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:08.420
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:13.260
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:20.260
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.520
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.520
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:33.610
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:36.610
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:42.830
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:49.130
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:55.460
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:01.430
Condition Green

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.900
Attention bank robber:
You are surrounded.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:23.160
This is your last warning.
Exit your Labor immediately.

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:40.130
Move in.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.010
But...

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.800
We have no choice.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.010
Can't you...

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:46.390
Don't worry, sir.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.680
Shouldn't you...

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.390
Machines 1 and 2: Charge.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.030
If he resists, use the baton.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.200
<i>I don't think it will come to that.</i>

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:12.670
Press him back.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:34.650
That's enough.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:43.070
Division 1 Makes Swift Arrest

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:43.070
Praise for
the New AV-Zero

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.110
Care for some tea?

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.280
Yes, thank you.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.950
The media has certainly given
the Zero a warm reception.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.540
You must feel quite fortunate.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.500
Are you afraid of
the comparisons to Division 2?

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:56.460
My team does require
a delicate touch, at times.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:00.210
Machine 1 is in the pink.
How's number 2?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.050
Running smoothly.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:04.430
Great! Cut the current
and put it in standby.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.890
What's wrong, Ota?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.060
Lt. Kumagami.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.110
Why the long face?

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:18.150
It's nothing.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.360
Have they shaken your confidence?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:24.780
Should you be comparing
yourself to the Zero?

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:31.000
Confidence? The best I can do
is to bull my way through.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.460
But I've always had my pride.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:40.170
Good. We have different styles,
but common goals.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.430
Don't let the media
get under your skin.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.720
Cheer up.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.140
Oh, there you are.
They're here, Shinshi.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.390
What's up?

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:59.770
Ota, want to come
to my place for dinner?

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:01.690
It's a real home-cooked meal!

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:03.400
His wife is cooking.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.990
Tamiko is really excited.
I hope she doesn't get carried away.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.120
Lt. Kumagami, will you come?

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.500
I'd be honored.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:16.920
Great! That'll keep Ota under control!

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.000
What?

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.920
Nothing.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:21.960
What about Shinohara and Izumi?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:25.130
I think they need some time alone.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.010
Have you seen Noa?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:34.980
She's missing.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.900
Pub Izumi

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:50.870
Hi! I was just closing up.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.040
The sashimi's fresh.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:01.340
Thanks.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.680
There's also some fresh fish roe.

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.970
She's fine! Sit down.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.850
She just got here!
They don't feed her a thing out in Tokyo!

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.810
Mom's lost weight.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.600
Yeah, and what she lost, I gained.

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.900
You shouldn't be putting
on weight at your age.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.190
Again with the age thing?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.610
Relax. I won't age a bit
until you get married.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.910
Then maybe you'll
be like this forever.

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:39.120
So how is it?

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:40.080
What?

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:41.500
Your job.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:47.380
It's great! I love my job,
my coworkers are all great,

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.430
and every day is interesting and fun.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:54.930
I see.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:05.650
I haven't challenged you in a while.
Bring a glass, Mom!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.500
What are you doing?

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.000
What's it look like?

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:25.460
Why are you polishing
Izumi's Ingram?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:30.380
I'm her partner. Maybe you
should try it once in a while.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:39.390
Special Vehicles, Second Section.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.900
Oh, hello. This is Goto.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.780
What's up, Mr. Sakaki?

00:07:56.240 --> 00:08:02.290
Odd. Why are they suddenly
taking care of their machines?

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:03.960
Aren't they cute?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.920
Shinohara, come here.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.910
If you cry, Alphonse won't
be able to move on.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:39.870
Move on?

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.830
Sooner or later,
the time comes for everybody.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:46.920
We need to bravely
see them on their way.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:51.760
But he's all alone in the ground.
I feel so sorry for him.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.970
Dogs don't live as long as people do.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.470
You have to appreciate them
for the brief time they're with you.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.930
Don't feel sorry for Alphonse.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.140
But...

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:10.020
If you cry, Alphonse will always
try to stay with you.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:13.650
He'll be there with a worried look
on his face, whimpering.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:19.200
Don't worry about Alphonse.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.000
Okay, Noa?

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:53.480
It's the same.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.920
Uh...

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.080
Did you need a break?

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:04.550
Dad, I have to go back to Tokyo.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:07.640
Already? You just got here!

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:10.810
You must get that
from your mother's side.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.440
The Captain sends his thanks.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:20.320
Let him know that
all of us are grateful.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:23.950
Ma, I'm taking them to Chitose.
Mind the shop.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.240
I think we can just
make the last flight.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:30.910
You have quite a father.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.050
Miss Izumi!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:45.640
A mobilization?

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.850
Sorry to do this to you,
just as you get back.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.430
Don't worry. Situation?

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.100
A terrorist at the Kawasaki Complex.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:56.400
Division 1 is there.
Our team is on the way.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.040
Noa!

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.410
A fire here would be catastrophic.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.950
Don't use either
the cannon or the baton.

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:48.780
<i>Roger.</i>

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.740
Ota, did you copy that?

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:51.910
<i>Roger.</i>

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.510
Can you find him?

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:08.390
I'll do what I can,
but this place is one big junkyard.

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:12.060
He picked a perfect place to hide.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.730
Do what you can. The helicopter
and Division 1 are also looking.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:18.940
Captain.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:21.610
I'm sorry I made you worry.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.740
What, me worry?

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:27.740
Izumi.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:35.790
We don't have time to talk.
There's a terrorist hiding in there.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:40.130
He's desperate and very dangerous,
so be careful.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:41.040
Can you do it?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.210
Of course.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:56.890
It's my duty to push you to the very end,
without pause or regret.

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:01.940
Ingram pilot: All green. Hiromi, deck up.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.080
<i>Your gun has been unloaded.</i>

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:28.800
This could all depend on whether
the Ingram or Zero finds him first.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:29.760
Gomioka?

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.970
<i>No sign of him yet.</i>

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:34.560
<i>Captain, what if the terrorist has fled</i>?

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.680
<i>Then you'll find an empty Labor.</i>

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:37.640
<i>Don't drop your guard.</i>

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:53.370
Lt. Kumagami, I'd like you
to watch the monitors for me.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:57.370
<i>Roger, Officer Ota.</i>
<i>Keep your eyes peeled.</i>

00:15:17.470 --> 00:15:18.060
Wait!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:22.600
<i>What</i>?

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:26.020
Sorry, I thought I saw movement.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.950
Look right!
It's a Labor's heat signature!

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:34.910
There he is!

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:46.750
Damn you!

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:50.010
No! Shooting here would be suicide!

00:15:56.970 --> 00:16:00.560
Target located. Proceeding toward
location 2-12/2-11.

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.350
Captain, I'm taking the mini-Patrol!

00:16:20.160 --> 00:16:20.660
Got him!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.850
Lt. Gomioka, it's heading your way!

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.100
<i>Roger. Give me backup.</i>

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:34.030
Yuki, no! You can't use the baton!

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.110
<i>But...</i>

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:35.610
Stand aside!

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:47.870
<i>Are you all right</i>?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:50.130
Don't worry, this always happens!

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.670
Halt, you villain!

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:56.010
Yuki, after him!

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.060
<i>Asuma, do you read me</i>?

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.230
What?

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:10.690
What does a Crabman weigh?

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:12.190
What are you up to?

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.230
<i>Just tell me.</i>

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.780
Fully equipped? Around 13 tons.

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:19.030
I can do it.

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:23.830
Hey, Noa!

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.210
Noa!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:59.200
Noa, are you all right?

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:01.660
Oh, no!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:07.120
Alphonse broke his knees!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.580
You overdid it again.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:12.710
But I got my man.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.010
Was the Chief here?

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.600
Intelligence isn't his strong point.

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:29.430
Did he mention the reorganization?

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:30.440
He did.

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:34.690
I give up! Okay, what did he decide?

00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:37.650
We'll keep things as they are, for now.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:41.240
Sometimes he makes
surprisingly intelligent decisions.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:45.780
One more thing, they've finally
picked a name for the Zero.

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:46.780
What?

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.870
AV-0: Peacemaker.

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:53.040
Peacemaker?
A maker of peace. It's perfect.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.670
Yeah.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.140
Didn't you bring
the reserve batteries?

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:10.480
The mobilization
was a complete sprint.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:14.690
Well, Shige, I guess I'll have
to leave the Zero in your hands.

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:19.690
Mr. Sakaki...

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:24.110
I've really enjoyed piloting the Ingram.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:30.790
It's kind of hard for me
to say this, but...

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:33.790
Please take good care of him.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:39.550
I think the Ingram may be
the last machine for me.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.590
The technology's changing
too quickly these days.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:46.340
Officer Izumi.

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.180
That was quite a throw.

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:55.400
By now, I have a pretty good idea
of what Alphonse can do.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:20:56.690
Ah, of course.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:20:59.860
I look forward to working
more with you.

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:10.290
We're on standby alert
until tomorrow.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:14.750
Want to see a movie?

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.210
You've changed.

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:23.630
Yes, I have.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:26.130
That's good.

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:56.220
arashi ga itsushika owatta

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:56.220
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:03.980
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni

00:22:58.310 --> 00:23:03.980
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:05.900
arawareta

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:05.900
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:11.410
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:11.410
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:19.710
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru

00:23:13.240 --> 00:23:19.710
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:29.470
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa

00:23:22.170 --> 00:23:29.470
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:35.390
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:35.390
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:44.560
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:44.560
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:50.030
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de

00:23:44.690 --> 00:23:50.030
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:53.660
ima hiraku yo

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:53.660
right now before our eyes.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:07.340
Good work!

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:12.720
This story is fiction...

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:12.720
but in 10 years, who knows?
